second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was the Coastal Highway expanded to four lanes?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 96, \"text\": \"at times, especially during weekends and holidays, when many Israelis travel north for vacation.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 97, \"end\": 235, \"text\": \"The first section of the highway between Tel Aviv and Netanya was built in the early 1950s as a two lane road with at-grade intersections.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 236, \"end\": 337, \"text\": \"The next section was built later that decade, extending the highway north to Olga Junction in Hadera.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 338, \"end\": 385, \"text\": \"This section was also built as a two lane road.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 386, \"end\": 516, \"text\": \"In 1965 the highway was widened to four lanes between Tel Aviv and Hadera, however grade separations were not built at this point.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"start\": 517, \"end\": 582, \"text\": \"The last section of the highway, between Olga Junction and Haifa,\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 68, \"text\": \"one-way in the downtown area, a change that was implemented by 1948.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 69, \"end\": 238, \"text\": \"Traffic volume in Ocean City increased even more following the completion of the Chesapeake Bay Bridge in 1952, leading to expansion of the city's north–south arterials.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 239, \"end\": 299, \"text\": \"MD 378 was widened along its entire length in 1951 and 1952.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 300, \"end\": 374, \"text\": \"MD 528 was widened to four lanes along its entire length in 1953 and 1954.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 375, \"end\": 456, \"text\": \"Both state highways were extended to their present southern termini at that time.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d01\", \"start\": 457, \"end\": 572, \"text\": \"The first portion of MD 528 to be expanded to a divided highway was around the intersection with MD 90; the highway\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0216-21b1c5e362c8:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Coastal Highway\", \"scope\": \"between Tel Aviv and Hadera\", \"claim\": \"In 1965 the highway was widened to four lanes between Tel Aviv and Hadera.\", \"answer\": \"1965\", \"quote\": \"In 1965 the highway was widened to four lanes between Tel Aviv and Hadera, however grade separations were not built at this point.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"1965\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"1965\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
